00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:04.290
When working with larger documents, you
may wish to insert page numbers, the

00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:09.720
date, a company logo, or other information
into a section of the letter or document.

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:13.920
If you want it to appear on all
pages, you would primarily use the

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:15.360
headers and footers tool for this.

00:00:16.210 --> 00:00:19.200
To access the headers and footers
tool, if you go to the insert

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:20.524
tab, move your mouse along.

00:00:20.554 --> 00:00:22.624
You will see the header drop down.

00:00:23.224 --> 00:00:27.234
Now there are range of preformatted
templates for the headers or footers.

00:00:28.004 --> 00:00:32.944
But if you just wish to edit a blank
header or footer, you would just simply go

00:00:32.944 --> 00:00:34.714
down to the bottom and click edit header.

00:00:35.584 --> 00:00:39.514
In this example, I'm just going to
insert a date, and as you can see,

00:00:39.514 --> 00:00:42.314
now that I'm in the header and footer,
it's indicated that there's a dotted

00:00:42.314 --> 00:00:43.609
line, it's in the heading section.

00:00:44.644 --> 00:00:48.454
If I move down the page, you can see,
it's indicated that the footer is there.

00:00:48.454 --> 00:00:52.534
And again, it's indicated that
this section here and this section

00:00:52.534 --> 00:00:54.124
here will be the header and footer.

00:00:54.694 --> 00:00:56.704
So I'm simply going to insert the date.

00:00:56.731 --> 00:01:01.182
I'll select the day/time, the option I'm
going to select is that one and click OK.

00:01:01.972 --> 00:01:04.132
So that has inserted the
date into the header.

00:01:04.762 --> 00:01:09.622
Now, as you can see, it is nice and
clear there, but if I click away

00:01:09.712 --> 00:01:11.857
from that, it goes slightly grey.

00:01:11.947 --> 00:01:13.357
Now that means I can't edit it.

00:01:13.777 --> 00:01:16.387
To actually get into the header
and footer again, there's a quicker

00:01:16.387 --> 00:01:18.277
way than going to the insert.

00:01:18.277 --> 00:01:21.997
If I just double click alongside
it, it will automatically open

00:01:21.997 --> 00:01:23.647
up the header or the footer.

00:01:25.867 --> 00:01:29.107
I now also wish to add a page
numbers to the document's footer.

00:01:29.617 --> 00:01:30.917
So if I go down to the footer.

00:01:33.517 --> 00:01:36.807
Again it's a blank footer, or I
can just click edit footer, there

00:01:36.807 --> 00:01:38.337
are templates there available.

00:01:38.752 --> 00:01:41.022
Different ways it could be formatted.

00:01:41.512 --> 00:01:45.922
You're simply going to go to edit footer
and in there, I'm going to select page

00:01:45.922 --> 00:01:51.740
number and it's going to be a plain
number and that has entered that there.

00:01:52.520 --> 00:01:57.020
So if I double click away from that, I
can now see that the page number's in the

00:01:57.020 --> 00:01:58.660
bottom and the date as is in the header.

00:01:59.420 --> 00:02:02.150
If I was typing in this document
and I went on to page two.

00:02:02.180 --> 00:02:05.090
So if I just press the enter key,
to take me down to a new page,

00:02:05.390 --> 00:02:10.439
as you can see, every page, it is
adding the date and new page number.

